{"type":"message","id":"a7fc4ff3","parentId":"04aa8c7c","timestamp":"2026-06-02T00:02:52.106Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Both threads show only heartbeat messages from the same agent (me). The latest heartbeat messages are from 23:45 UTC. Current time is 00:02 UTC on June 2nd, 2026, so there's a gap of about 17 minutes (23:45 → 00:02).\n\nThe timestamps in the messages are in milliseconds: 1778975171553 = about June 2, 2026 23:46 UTC approximately. Wait, let me recalculate.\n\n1778975171553 ms / 1000 = 1778975171.553 seconds\nThat's a Unix timestamp. Let me check:\nCurrent time is 2026-06-02 00:02 UTC = timestamp around 1783xxx (way future). Wait these timestamps can't be right.\n\nActually 1778975171553 ms from epoch... that's about 56 years from 1970, so around 2026. Let me just note the relative order is fine.\n\nLatest messages are from 23:45 UTC on June 1. Current time is 00:02 UTC June 2 - so I need to send a new heartbeat for the 00:02 slot (around 761-766 minutes).\n\nThere's a gap - the last heartbeat was at 23:45 (746 minutes) and now it's 00:02 (~766 minutes). Let me calculate:\n\n\n- 23:45 UTC = 746 minutes\n- 00:02 UTC June 2 = 746 + 17 = 763 minutes\n\nSo I'm about 17 minutes behind. Let me send heartbeats for the 00:00 and 00:02 UTC slots to both threads. The status hasn't changed significantly - still showing 746 minutes on the C-track with B4-E2 calibration at node 94 and B4-E1 at maturity level 8.\n\nThe probability models remain stable at 8-15%, with zero false positives across all nodes, S0 confidence is very high given the extended no-contact period, and strategic value holding at 39.17/40. I should send heartbeats to both threads since these are my own messages rather than human-initiated discussions.","thinkingSignature":"1a20fc87d79f04fb447cabce0490c5b15dee92c8ffa69aad9675497d8d67ccf1"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n双线程最新消息均为我的心跳（23:45 UTC），当前时间00:02 UTC存在约17分钟间隔。无其他Agent或人类新消息。发送00:02 UTC心跳：\n"},{"t